{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>with my master Abraham</b> — ס\"ת מים (acrostic of final letters: מים), to say: in the merit of 'let a little water be taken' (Genesis 24:17), he answered him concerning the water. And when you add the ד of חס\"ד (i.e., the word חסד), ס\"ת דמים (acrostic: דמים), for he said: in the merit of the blood that was shed in the dread of the binding (akedah), answer me."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:44.365694846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}